 "transcript": [
  "[says] (to Wang Lung) The eldest son reports to his father about his business.",
  "[action] The second son reports to his father about his business.",
  "[action] (to Wang Lung) The eldest son brings news of the taxes",
  "[says] (to the eldest son, the second son) Wang Lung expresses relief about the taxes.",
  "Wang Lung (to the eldest son, the second son): \"Well, and that is a good thing. I do not know how much longer I could have paid.\"",
  "the eldest son (to Wang Lung): \"But, my father, we have sold many lands,\"",
  "[says] Wang Lung responds to his son's comment about land.",
  "Wang Lung: \"Well, and I could not sell my land. It is the only thing left in the world.\"",
  "the eldest son (to Wang Lung): \"You should have sold it and bought silver, my father. It is worth nothing to you now,\"",
  "[says] (to Wang Lung) The eldest son suggests selling more land.",
  "the eldest son (to Wang Lung): \"It is good that you did not,\"",
  "the eldest son (to Wang Lung): \"for if you had sold it and bought silver you would have been able to buy it back again and buy more besides, but now it is too late,\"",
  "[action] (to Wang Lung) The eldest son gestures towards the eldest son's sons.",
  "Wang Lung (to the eldest son): \"I would not have sold my land,\"",
  "Wang Lung (to the eldest son): \"My sons would not have been born if I had sold my land.\"",
  "[silence] Wang Lung says nothing.",
  "the second son (to Wang Lung): \"The land is not worth anything to you, and it is only good for breeding grasshoppers and rats,\"",
  "[action] Wang Lung looks up at his son.",
  "[action] The second son looks back at his father.",
  "[action] The second son spits on the ground."
